      use: 'À covers at, to, in and for. The form you pick depends on the gender and number of the noun that follows: à la for a feminine singular, au for a masculine singular, à l’ when the noun starts with a vowel or a silent h, aux for any plural. These carry every location, direction and destination on the test.',
      avoid: 'Never write “à le” or “à les” — the contraction to au and aux is compulsory. Do not use à with a person’s home; that is chez: je vais chez le médecin. And with cities à stands alone: à Paris, not “à la Paris”.',
