      use: 'Il y a states that something exists, and it never changes for number: il y a un restaurant, il y a beaucoup de monde. Ask about existence with it — il y a du lait dans le réfrigérateur ? Followed by a time and que it measures how long something has been going on: il y a un an que je travaille ici. With weather it reports conditions: il y a du soleil aujourd’hui.',
      avoid: 'It has no plural form — never “ils y ont”. In the negative it becomes il n’y a pas de: il n’y a pas de lait. And keep it apart from the past marker il y a deux ans, “two years ago”, where there is no que.',
