      use: 'Every negation keeps the same frame: ne before the verb, the second word after it. Swap pas for plus, jamais, rien, personne or nulle part to change the meaning. Ne … ni … ni negates two things at once, and ne … que is not a negative at all — it means “only”.',
      avoid: 'After ni … ni and after ne … que the article rules change: il ne boit ni café ni thé drops the article entirely, and il ne mange que des légumes keeps des because que means only, not not. Ne still shrinks to n’ before a vowel: il n’écoute rien. Do not stack pas with another negation — “ne pas jamais” is wrong.',
