      use: 'Exercise 13 fills in dire: Paul dit, les professeurs disent, elle dit, nous disons, tu dis, ma mère dit, les parents disent, Pierre dit, vous dites, mon professeur dit. Exercise 15 asks you to conjugate five to ten of these and read the meaning of all: attendre (to wait), vendre (to sell), perdre (to lose), répondre (to answer), entendre (to hear), comprendre (to understand), rendre (to give back), défendre (to defend, to forbid), descendre (to go down), dépendre (to depend), répandre (to spread), fondre (to melt), tendre (to stretch), apprendre (to learn), surprendre (to surprise), battre (to beat), connaître (to know), prendre (to take), apparaître (to appear), mettre (to put), naître (to be born).',
      avoid: 'Not all of them share one pattern. Attendre, vendre, perdre, répondre, entendre, rendre, défendre, descendre, dépendre, répandre, fondre and tendre are regular. Prendre, apprendre, comprendre and surprendre drop the d in the plural. Battre and mettre double the t. Connaître, apparaître and naître take the circumflex before a t and a double s in the plural.',
