   "use": "The near future — “going to” — for plans and things about to happen: ce soir, demain, ce week-end, cette année. Conjugate aller in the present and keep the second verb in the infinitive. It is the simplest way to talk about the future in a TCF speaking task.",
   "avoid": "Only aller is conjugated: je vais manger, never “je vais mange”. The negative wraps aller, not the infinitive: je ne vais pas manger. An object pronoun goes before the infinitive: je vais le faire, je vais te voir.",
