   "use": "Endings: -s, -s, -t, -ons, -ez, -vent. Recevoir (to receive) is the model for concevoir (to conceive), décevoir (to disappoint), apercevoir (to catch sight of) and percevoir (to perceive). Devoir means must, to have to: je dois étudier. Redevoir (to owe again) follows devoir. Apercevoir is physical — j’aperçois un oiseau; percevoir is abstract — je perçois une tension.",
   "avoid": "The cédille: reçois, aperçois, déçoit — the c needs ç before o to keep the s sound; without it “recois” would read “reh-KWAH”. No cédille before e: nous recevons. After devoir the next verb stays in the infinitive: je dois étudier, not “je dois étudie”.",
