   "use": "The warm-up mixes the three tenses of the course so far. Read each English sentence, decide the time (habit, finished past, plan), then pick the tense: présent for habits (elle lit tous les jours), passé composé for finished actions (il a visité Paris l’été dernier), aller + infinitive for plans (nous allons à la plage demain is the present of aller with a time marker).",
   "avoid": "English “have travelled” is not a French present perfect: write ils sont allés en Italie deux fois. “She wanted to learn” describes a wish, so the imparfait elle voulait apprendre is more natural than elle a voulu. Jouer de for instruments (de la guitare), jouer à for sports (au soccer in Canada, au football in France). Breakfast is prendre le petit-déjeuner, not manger. “He has studied French for three years” with pendant means the studying is over; if he still studies it, write il étudie le français depuis trois ans.",
