   "use": "Every country has a gender and normally takes the definite article: le Canada, la France, les Philippines. The quick test: a name ending in -e is feminine (la Belgique, la Chine, l’Australie); anything else is masculine (le Japon, le Maroc, le Pérou). Learn the six masculine exceptions in -e by heart. All continents end in -e and are feminine.",
