   "modelEn": "My favourite season is autumn, especially in Canada. In September and October the weather is mild, between ten and eighteen degrees. It is sometimes windy and cloudy, but the sky is often blue and the sun shines. The trees turn red, yellow and orange, and it is stunning. At weekends I go hiking in the parks with friends. In the evenings it gets colder and colder, so I have a hot tea and read a book at home. In November it rains more often, and sometimes it is already snowing. Even so, I love this season because it is peaceful and very beautiful. It is also the ideal time to study French on long evenings.",
   "sound": "mah seh-ZOHN pray-fay-RAY, seh loh-TUN, sewr-TOO oh kah-nah-DAH. ahn sep-TAHM-bruh ay ahn ok-TOH-bruh, eel feh DOO : AHN-truh DEESS ay dee-ZWEET duh-GRAY. eel ee ah par-FWAH dew VAHN ay day NWAHZH, meh soo-VAHN luh SYEL eh BLUH ay luh soh-LAY BREE-yuh. lay zar-bruh duh-vee-EN ROOZH, ZHOHN ay oh-RAHNZH : seh mah-nyee-FEEK. luh wee-KEND, zhuh feh duh lah rahn-doh-NAY ah-vek may zah-MEE dahn lay PARK. luh SWAHR, eel feh duh plew zahn plew FRWAH, ah-LOR zhuh bwah uhn TAY SHOH ay zhuh lee uhn LEE-vruh ah lah meh-ZOHN. ahn noh-VAHM-bruh, eel PLUH plew soo-VAHN ay par-FWAH eel NEZH day-ZHAH. poor-TAHN, ZHEM set seh-ZOHN, pars-kel eh KAHLM ay treh BEL. seh toh-SEE luh moh-MAHN ee-day-AL poor ay-tew-dee-AY luh frahn-SEH pahn-DAHN duh lohng swah-RAY."
