Object.assign(PROD_DATA[5].ee[0], {"model":"Bonjour Madame,\n\nJe vous écris parce que je suis malade et je ne peux pas venir au cours de jeudi. J’ai de la fièvre, j’ai mal à la tête et le médecin dit que j’ai besoin de repos pendant deux jours.\n\nEst-ce que je peux venir au cours de vendredi à la place ? Je vais lire la leçon et faire mes devoirs à la maison. Je vous envoie mes exercices par e-mail samedi.\n\nMerci beaucoup pour votre compréhension et à bientôt,\nMariz","modelEn":"Dear Madam, I am writing because I am ill and cannot come to Thursday’s class. I have a temperature and a headache, and the doctor says I need two days’ rest. Might I attend Friday’s class instead? I will read the lesson and do my homework at home, and I will email you my exercises on Saturday. Thank you very much for your understanding. Best wishes, Mariz","sound":"bohn-ZHOOR mah-DAHM, zhuh voo zay-KREE pars-kuh zhuh swee mah-LAHD ay zhuh nuh puh pah vuh-NEER oh KOOR duh zhuh-DEE. zhay duh lah FYEH-vruh, zhay MAHL ah lah TET ay luh mayd-SAN DEE kuh zhay buh-ZWAN duh ruh-POH pahn-DAHN duh ZHOOR. es-kuh zhuh puh vuh-NEER oh KOOR duh vahn-druh-DEE ah lah PLAHS ? zhuh veh LEER lah luh-SOHN ay fehr may duh-VWAHR ah lah meh-ZOHN. zhuh voo zahn-VWAH may zeg-zehr-SEES par ee-MEL sahm-DEE. mehr-SEE boh-KOO poor voh-truh kohn-pray-ahn-SYOHN ay ah bee-an-TOH, mah-REEZ"});

// Sentence-aligned English — one English sentence per French sentence
(() => { const E = {"4.eo.1":["Good morning, do you run any beginner courses?","What time do the classes start?","How many people are there in each group?","Where exactly is the school?","And how much does it cost per month?"],"5.ee.1":["My day gets off to an early start.","I wake at six and get up straight away.","I shower, brush my teeth and have breakfast: a coffee and some bread with fruit.","After that I head to the office.","I work from nine to five and have lunch at noon with my colleagues.","In the afternoon there is often a meeting.","In the evening I either exercise or go for a walk in the park.","After dinner I spend twenty-five minutes on French, listening to dialogues and repeating them aloud.","I go to bed at ten, because I need eight hours’ sleep."],"5.ee.2":["Both opinions address the same issue: health.","According to the first, fixed mealtimes build a good habit.","That is true: when I have lunch at noon every day, I don’t get hungry between meals and I work better in the afternoon.","That said, the second opinion also has a point.","Every person is different, and so is every day.","On Saturdays, for example, I sleep in and have no appetite at seven.","In my view, fixed times make sense during the working week, with more flexibility at weekends.","The key thing is to avoid too much sugar and drink enough water.","In short, habits help, but they should not become an absolute rule."],"6.eo.1":["Good morning, do you offer swimming lessons for adults?","What time are the classes?","How much is the registration fee?","Is a medical certificate required?","And where exactly is the centre?"],"6.ee.1":["I live in a large city by the sea.","There is plenty to do.","In the morning you can visit the market: the fruit and vegetables are fresh and inexpensive.","Next to the market there is a park where children play and people ride their bikes.","The city centre has a museum, a cinema and a public library.","In the evening the restaurants open at seven, and you can eat very well for twenty euros.","When the weather is good, I go to the beach with friends and we take a walk.","My city isn’t perfect — there is far too much traffic — but I really enjoy living there."],"6.ee.2":["Both opinions put forward serious arguments.","The first is right on one point: at school a teacher corrects your mistakes and explains the rules.","What is more, being in a group forces you to speak and to listen to others.","That said, the second is also fair.","With an app you practise every day, at a time of your choosing, and repeat as often as you like.","I, for example, listen to dialogues on the bus and repeat them aloud.","In my view, there is no need to choose.","The best approach combines a course for grammar and correction with twenty-five minutes of daily self-study for pronunciation and vocabulary.","In conclusion, school provides structure and independent work builds the habit.","Together, they deliver results."],"7.eo.0":["This weekend I intend to take things a little easier.","On Saturday morning I’ll fit in a workout and then pick up the groceries at the market.","In the afternoon I’ll set aside two hours for French, since I need to prepare for the TCF.","On Sunday, weather permitting, we’ll head out for a family walk.","In the evening I’ll give my parents a call back home in the Philippines."],"7.eo.1":["Good morning, I’m looking to travel to Paris in September.","What flights do you have out of Toronto?","How much is a return ticket?","Is the hotel close to the city centre?","Is breakfast included?","What is the weather usually like in Paris in September?","Can I cancel free of charge?","Which tours do you offer?","Of these two hotels, which one is quieter?","Do I need to pay straight away?","Could you email me the details?"],"7.ee.0":["Hi Marc, I’ve just arrived in Nice!","The weather is glorious — twenty-eight degrees.","The hotel is right next to the beach.","Tomorrow I’m going to explore the old town and have a meal in a little restaurant that serves fish.","It’s forecast to rain on Wednesday, so I’ll go to the museum instead.","What about you — what are you up to this week?","Speak soon, Mariz"],"7.ee.2":["Both opinions concern the best time of year to travel.","According to the first, summer is ideal: it is warm, the days are long and you can go to the beach.","That is true, particularly for families, since the children are off school.","However, the second opinion is also valid.","In summer, flights and hotels are very expensive and the beaches are packed.","Off-season — in autumn, for example — the weather is often mild, there are fewer tourists and you can visit museums at your leisure.","In my view, if you have the choice, it is better to go in spring or autumn.","You pay less, see more of the city and find it easier to talk to people.","In conclusion, summer is pleasant, but off-season travel is the smarter choice for your budget."],"8.eo.2":["In my view, it isn’t that simple.","On the one hand, when it’s warm all year round you can go out, head to the beach and exercise outdoors.","That’s the case in the Philippines, for instance.","On the other hand, the seasons have their advantages too.","In Canada, autumn is stunning, and in winter the snow means you can go skiing.","What’s more, the heat can make working hard going.","All in all, I believe every climate has its merits, but personally I rather enjoy the change of seasons."],"8.ee.2":["Both opinions concern the place of the phone in a restaurant.","According to the first, you should switch your phone off.","That is true: a meal is a time to talk with the people at your table.","When you look at your screen, you are not listening to others, and it is rude to the waiter.","That said, the second opinion also has a point.","With a phone you can read customer reviews before choosing a restaurant, book a table and pay quickly.","For me, as someone who works in finance, paying by phone is extremely convenient.","In my view, the answer is balance.","You can use your phone before and after the meal, but during dinner it is better to put it away in your bag.","In conclusion, the phone is a useful tool, but it should never replace conversation."],"9.ee.1":["Last summer I spent a week in Quebec City with my family.","We arrived on a Friday evening and stayed in a small hotel in the old town.","On Saturday we visited the Château Frontenac and climbed up onto the ramparts.","The weather was glorious all week.","On Sunday we took the ferry across the river and tried poutine for the first time.","My son loved it!","On the last day I went to a bookshop on my own and bought two books in French.","I chatted with the bookseller for twenty minutes and understood everything.","That is why this trip has stayed with me: I felt my French was becoming genuinely useful."],"9.ee.2":["Both opinions address the same question: when should you see a doctor?","According to the first, you should go straight away.","That is true of certain symptoms: a high fever, chest pain or a fall.","Last year my father fell and waited three days; in the end it turned out he had broken his wrist.","That said, the second opinion also has a point.","For a mild cold or a headache, rest, water and a little patience are often enough.","What is more, surgeries are very busy, and you sometimes wait a long time for an appointment.","In my view, you have to listen to your body.","If the pain is severe or lasts more than three days, you should see a doctor.","Otherwise, you can wait and ask the pharmacist for advice.","In conclusion, common sense is the best doctor."],"11.ee.1":["In five years’ time, I hope my life will have changed a great deal.","First, I will speak French fluently.","I will have passed the TCF and I will work for a fintech company, building artificial-intelligence tools.","It will be a fascinating job.","Next, I will probably live in Montreal or Ottawa, two bilingual cities.","I will rent a bright flat close to the metro, because I don’t want to waste time commuting.","Finally, in my free time I will go hiking in summer and skiing in winter.","I will travel too: I will spend three weeks in France and visit Paris and Provence.","Of course I will have to work hard, but I believe I can do it."],"11.ee.2":["Both opinions concern the best way to travel.","According to the first, the train is preferable.","That is true: you leave from the city centre, arrive in the city centre, and can work or read on the way.","What is more, trains pollute far less than planes.","That said, the second opinion also has a point.","Over long distances — between Toronto and Vancouver, for example — flying is much faster: five hours instead of four days.","Plane tickets are also sometimes cheaper.","In my view, it all depends on the distance.","For a journey of under four hours, I will always take the train.","To cross the country or the ocean, I will choose to fly.","In conclusion, both will remain useful, but rail will no doubt become more important for the environment."]};
 for (const id in E) { const [d, k, i] = id.split('.'); PROD_DATA[d][k][+i].modelEn = E[id].join(' '); PROD_DATA[d][k][+i].enLines = E[id]; } })();
